\ Spitfire: photographic reconnaissance. The PR IV carried two F24 cameras
\ behind the pilot as a split vertical pair: both look down, each tilted to
\ its own side of the track so their frames overlap and together cover a
\ strip twice as wide. Each F24 here has the 20-inch lens and makes 5-inch
\ square exposures, 125 to a magazine (published), so a frame covers
\ 2 × atan(2.5 / 20), 14.25°, across; the tilt of 6° each way is an
\ estimate. The pilot opens the mud flaps over the lenses and starts the
\ intervalometer (C), which exposes a pair at the interval that gives 60%
\ overlap along the track at the height and speed, an estimate of the
\ setting, until the magazines are spent. Each exposure records where the
\ aircraft was and how it lay. After landing the film is developed (V): the
\ review draws each frame from that place, looking down through the lens,
\ in grey, and names the frames that caught the Tirpitz.
\
\ Flak defends the Tirpitz, Trondheim, Munkholmen and Værnes. Nothing fires
\ at an aircraft on the ground, nor from a site whose line to it the hills
\ cut. Each site's heavy battery, the 8.8 cm Flak 36 with its published
\ effective ceiling of 8,000 m, engages within an estimated 10 km while its
\ crews can follow the aircraft across the sky, at most an estimated 10° a
\ second: a burst a second, four guns at the published 15 to 20 rounds a
\ minute (four an estimate), near the aircraft; a burst within 60 m damages
\ it (an estimate), sometimes holing the radiator or the oil system. Low and
\ close, an aircraft crosses the sky faster than that and the heavy guns
\ lose it. Each site's light guns, the 2 cm Flak 38, engage within its
\ published 2,200 m at its published practical 180 rounds a minute and
\ 900 m/s, twelve aboard the Tirpitz and four at each other site
\ (estimates), aimed at the aircraft's lead to within 0.01 rad (as a rear
\ gunner's, an estimate); their rounds fly and hit as gunnery.telic's do.
\ Time can run four or sixteen times as fast (T) for the long crossing.

2.5 20 / atan 2 * constant lens-angle
6 PI 180 / * constant split-angle
125 constant magazine-exposures
0.6 constant photo-overlap
8000 constant flak-ceiling
10000 constant flak-reach
10 constant flak-tracking-rate
60 constant flak-lethal-distance
2200 constant light-flak-reach
180 constant light-flak-rate
900 constant light-flak-velocity
0x303030 constant flak-colour

variable photos
[ ] to photos
variable flak-bursts
[ ] to flak-bursts

\ the photographs and the flak forgotten, for a new flight
: reset-reconnaissance ( -- )
	| ^photos ^flak-bursts |
	[ ] to photos
	[ ] to flak-bursts ;

\ a camera's attitude: the aircraft's turned to look straight down, the top of the frame toward the nose, then tilted to one side, -1 left and 1 right
: camera-attitude ( attitude side -- attitude' )
	| attitude side |
	attitude :right PI 2 / turn-attitude :up side split-angle * turn-attitude ;

\ whether a point shows in a camera's frame from a position: in front of the lens and inside its angle both ways
: in-frame? ( point position attitude -- flag )
	| point position attitude |
	attitude point position v- ground>attitude spread to ahead to rising to across
	lens-angle 2 / tan to edge
	ahead 0 > across abs ahead edge * < and rising abs ahead edge * < and ;

\ whether a photograph caught the Tirpitz: her bow, centre or stern in either camera's frame
: shows-tirpitz? ( photo -- flag )
	| photo |
	tirpitz-berth tirpitz-heading 0 0 120 placed to bow
	tirpitz-berth tirpitz-heading 0 0 -120 placed to stern
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		photo@attitude side camera-attitude to attitude
		[ bow tirpitz-berth stern ] ( point | point photo@position attitude in-frame? ) any?
	) any? ;

\ the intervalometer's step: when the interval has run, a pair exposed and its place recorded, the next interval set for 60% overlap at the height and the speed over the ground
: run-cameras ( elapsed -- )
	| elapsed ^photos |
	:cameras-running game@ not if exit then
	:exposures-left game@ 0 <= if
		false :cameras-running game!
		"THE MAGAZINES ARE SPENT" say
		exit
	then
	:exposure-timer game@ elapsed - :exposure-timer game!
	:exposure-timer game@ 0 > if exit then
	plane@position second 0 max2 to height
	plane@velocity spread to vz drop to vx
	vx sq vz sq + sqrt 30 max2 to ground-speed
	height lens-angle 2 / tan 2 * * 1 photo-overlap - * ground-speed / 1 max2 :exposure-timer game!
	photos { :position plane@position :attitude plane@attitude :time :flight-time game@ } add-last! drop
	:exposures-left game@ 1- :exposures-left game! ;

\ === the flak ===

\ the places the flak defends, each [ position light-guns ]
: flak-sites ( -- sites )
	[ [ tirpitz-berth 12 ] [ :munkholmen landmark-ground 4 ] [ :vaernes landmark-ground 4 ] [ :nidaros landmark-ground 4 ] ] ;

\ whether a site's guns, 5 m above the ground, see a point: no hill rises above the line between them at eleven points along it
: in-sight? ( site point -- flag )
	| site point |
	site first site 2 @i ground-height 5 + site second max2 to gun-height
	[ site first gun-height site 2 @i ] to gun
	[ 1 12 1 do k
		gun point k 12 / v-between to along
		along first along 2 @i ground-height along second <
	loop ] ( clear | clear ) all? ;

\ how fast, degrees a second, an aircraft crosses the sky as a site sees it: its speed across the line of sight over its distance
: crossing-rate ( site -- degrees )
	| site |
	plane@position site v- to offset
	offset v-length to range
	offset 1 range / v* to line
	plane@velocity line plane@velocity line v-dot v* v- v-length range 1 max2 / 180 * PI / ;

\ a heavy burst near the aircraft, which damages it when close
: heavy-burst ( -- )
	| ^flak-bursts |
	plane@position to aircraft
	aircraft [ random 0.5 - 300 * random 0.5 - 120 * random 0.5 - 300 * ] v+ plane@velocity 1.5 v* v+ to burst
	flak-bursts [ burst 4 ] add-last! drop
	burst aircraft v- v-length flak-lethal-distance < not if exit then
	plane@damage 15 + 100 min2 plane!damage
	"HIT BY FLAK" say
	random 0.3 < if
		plane@coolant-leak 0.01 + plane!coolant-leak
		"FLAK IN THE RADIATOR  -  GLYCOL LEAKING, WATCH THE TEMPERATURE" say
	then
	random 0.15 < if
		plane@oil-leak 0.005 + plane!oil-leak
		"FLAK IN THE OIL SYSTEM  -  WATCH THE OIL PRESSURE" say
	then ;

\ a site's light guns' rounds for a step: a salvo from the site at the aircraft's lead point
: light-salvo ( site guns dt -- )
	| site guns dt |
	{ :kind :flak :position site :attitude 0 heading-attitude :speed 0 } to battery
	battery plane light-flak-velocity lead-point site v- v-unit to direction
	salvos
	{ :position site :velocity direction light-flak-velocity v*
	  :rounds guns light-flak-rate * 60 / dt * :weight cannon-weight :spread rear-spread :travel 0 :age 0 :life 3
	  :target plane :credit :german :source "HIT BY LIGHT FLAK" }
	add-last! drop ;

\ the flak's step: the bursts fade over 4 s; nothing fires at an aircraft on the ground or crashed; each site that sees the aircraft fires its light guns within their reach, and its heavy battery, a burst a second, within its reach and under its ceiling while the aircraft crosses the sky no faster than the crews can follow
: run-flak ( dt -- )
	| dt ^flak-bursts |
	flak-bursts ( burst | [ burst first burst second dt - ] ) map ( burst | burst second 0 > ) filter to flak-bursts
	plane@on-ground plane@crashed or if exit then
	plane@position to aircraft
	flak-sites ( site |
		site spread to guns to place
		[ place first place first place 2 @i ground-height 5 + place 2 @i ] to gun
		aircraft gun v- v-length to range
		range flak-reach < if
			gun aircraft in-sight? if
				range light-flak-reach < if gun guns dt light-salvo then
				aircraft second flak-ceiling < gun crossing-rate flak-tracking-rate < and random dt < and if heavy-burst then
			then
		then
	) each ;

\ each burst a dark star of fourteen arms, six along the axes 20 m long and eight toward a cube's corners 14 m long, fading as it ages
: draw-flak ( -- )
	flak-bursts ( burst |
		burst first to centre
		new-sketch to puff
		[ [ 20 0 0 ] [ -20 0 0 ] [ 0 20 0 ] [ 0 -20 0 ] [ 0 0 20 ] [ 0 0 -20 ]
		  [ 8 8 8 ] [ 8 8 -8 ] [ 8 -8 8 ] [ 8 -8 -8 ] [ -8 8 8 ] [ -8 8 -8 ] [ -8 -8 8 ] [ -8 -8 -8 ] ] ( arm |
			puff [ centre centre arm v+ ] sketch-path
		) each
		puff flak-colour sky-colour burst second 4 / blended sketch>object draw-object
	) each ;

\ === the review of the film ===

\ the palette of a print: greys
: use-photograph ( -- )
	| ^sky-colour ^ground-colour ^water-colour ^lighting ^cloud-top-colour ^cloud-base-colour ^stars-showing ^hill-top-colour |
	0x9a9a9a to sky-colour
	0x6c6c6c to ground-colour
	0x9a9a9a to hill-top-colour
	0x2a2a2a to water-colour
	1 to lighting
	0xf0f0f0 to cloud-top-colour
	0xb0b0b0 to cloud-base-colour
	false to stars-showing ;

\ the frames that caught the Tirpitz, numbered from 1
: tirpitz-frames ( -- numbers )
	[ 0 photos size 1 do k
		photos k @i shows-tirpitz? if k 1+ then
	loop ] ;

\ one frame of the film: drawn from where it was exposed, through the camera's lens, a square print in grey in the middle of the view; under it the frame's number, the camera, the height and the time into the flight, and the frames that caught the Tirpitz
: draw-review ( scenery -- )
	| scenery ^focal-length ^monochrome |
	photos :review-index game@ @i to photo
	:review-side game@ to side
	photo@position to place
	place use-water-near
	place refresh-countryside
	place refresh-clouds
	use-photograph
	clear-visibility use-visibility
	view-height 2 / lens-angle 2 / tan / to focal-length
	true to monochrome
	place photo@attitude side camera-attitude look-from
	[ scenery countryside-collection ] bombers draw-scene
	false to monochrome
	420 to focal-length
	view-centre-x view-height 2 / - to left
	0 0 left view-height 0 fill-span
	left view-height + 0 view-width left - view-height - view-height 0 fill-span
	0 panel-top view-width screen-height panel-top - 0x101010 fill-span
	photo shows-tirpitz? if "TIRPITZ" else "" then to caught
	:review-index game@ 1+ photos size side 0 < if "LEFT" else "RIGHT" then place second 3.28084 * photo@time 60 / caught
	"FRAME {5} OF {4}   {3} CAMERA   {2:.0f} FT   {1:.0f} MIN   {0}" format to caption
	view-centre-x panel-top 20 + caption 0xffffff centred-print
	tirpitz-frames to caught-frames
	caught-frames size 0 = if
		"THE TIRPITZ IS IN NONE OF THE FRAMES"
	else
		caught-frames ( n | n "{0:.0f}" format ) map ", " join "THE TIRPITZ IS IN FRAMES {0}" format
	then to summary
	view-centre-x panel-top 50 + summary 0xffe080 centred-print
	view-centre-x panel-top 90 + "LEFT AND RIGHT: FRAMES   UP AND DOWN: CAMERA   ESC: DONE" dial-ink centred-print ;

\ a frame of the review: the keys and the d-pad move through the frames and between the cameras, escape ends it
: review-frame ( scenery -- )
	| scenery |
	photos size to n-photos
	:right key-pressed? :dpad-right 0 gamepad-pressed? or if :review-index game@ 1+ n-photos 1- min2 :review-index game! then
	:left key-pressed? :dpad-left 0 gamepad-pressed? or if :review-index game@ 1- 0 max2 :review-index game! then
	:up key-pressed? :dpad-up 0 gamepad-pressed? or if -1 :review-side game! then
	:down key-pressed? :dpad-down 0 gamepad-pressed? or if 1 :review-side game! then
	:escape key-pressed? :back 0 gamepad-pressed? or if false :reviewing game! exit then
	scenery draw-review ;

\ the panel's reconnaissance lines in the strip below it: the cameras, the target's bearing and its distance over the ground, in tenths of a mile within 10 miles, the time's pace
: draw-reconnaissance-panel ( target -- )
	| target |
	436 to x
	:cameras-running game@ if "CAMERAS RUNNING" else "CAMERAS OFF" then :exposures-left game@ "{1}  {0:.0f} LEFT" format to camera-line
	x floor-top 4 + camera-line :cameras-running game@ if 0xffe080 else dial-ink then draw-text
	target plane@position v- spread to dz drop to dx
	dx sq dz sq + sqrt 1609.34 / to miles
	miles [ dx 0 dz ] heading-of
	miles 10 < if "TARGET {0:03.0f} {1:.1f} MI" else "TARGET {0:03.0f} {1:.0f} MI" then format to target-line
	x floor-top 17 + target-line dial-ink draw-text
	:time-scale game@ 1 > if x floor-top 30 + :time-scale game@ "TIME x{0:.0f}" format 0xff9040 draw-text then ;
